D1 — Two Sum, modified
Classic version returned one pair. This one returns all of them.

nums = [2, 7, 11, 15, 3, 4, 8, 1]
target = 11

Return a list of tuples of every pair that sums to the target. Each pair only once — (3, 8) and (8, 3) are the same pair. Order within the tuple: smaller first.

Out loud before coding: what makes this O(n) instead of O(n²)?